 # dreb-session-appearance
 
-A local Dreb package for a more legible terminal UI and immediate visual separation between concurrent sessions.
+A local Dreb package for a more legible terminal UI and immediate visual separation between concurrent Dreb windows.
 
 ## Behavior
 
 - Applies the `pierre-readable` theme in memory, so it does not overwrite the persistent theme setting.
-- Uses stable semantic colors: cyan for primary actions, green for success, amber for warnings, rose for errors, violet for quoted/custom content, and brighter gray levels for footer metadata.
-- Derives a dark background hue from the Dreb session ID. A new session gets a pseudo-random hue; reopening the same session gets the same hue.
-- Applies the hue only to the terminal background with standard OSC 11; Dreb text colors stay explicit and the terminal's foreground/cursor settings are left alone.
-- Shows a compact colored session marker in the footer, such as `◆ Aegean · 205°`.
-- Recomputes the appearance after `/new`, `/resume`, or `/fork`.
-- Restores the terminal profile background on clean shutdown and before Dreb's default Ctrl+G external-editor or Ctrl+Z terminal handoffs; it reapplies on return/input.
-
-The canvas uses 55% HSL saturation and 13% lightness so concurrent sessions are visibly different while remaining dark. Automated checks require at least a 12:1 contrast ratio against the explicit `#F8FAFC` terminal text color for all generated hues. Secondary and tertiary theme text meet WCAG AA contrast against panel backgrounds.
+- Preserves a stable semantic palette: cyan for primary actions, green for success, amber for warnings, rose for errors, violet for quoted/custom content, and distinct syntax colors for code.
+- Selects one high-contrast identity color from a curated teal, orange, coral, lime, blue, and violet palette when a Dreb process starts. This identifies the running Dreb instance—not the active Dreb session.
+- Renders that identity as a persistent one-row, full-width stripe immediately above the editor and as a compact colored footer marker.
+- Keeps the identity color unchanged through `/new`, `/resume`, and `/fork`.
+- Leaves the Ghostty terminal profile canvas, text, cursor, and window chrome unchanged. Dreb cannot draw outside the Ghostty window; the in-app stripe is the durable orientation cue.
 
