-Restart Dreb after installation. The package is global, so it applies to new interactive sessions in every project. Headless, JSON, RPC, non-TTY, and `TERM=dumb` sessions do not receive terminal OSC sequences.
-
-## Opt out
-
-Disable only the terminal background while keeping the accessible Dreb theme:
-
-```bash
-DREB_SESSION_BACKGROUND=0 dreb
-```
-
-`NO_COLOR` also disables terminal color mutation. OSC background changes are disabled by default inside tmux, GNU screen, and Zellij because panes can share dynamic terminal colors; set `DREB_SESSION_BACKGROUND=1` to opt in there. An uncatchable `SIGKILL` cannot restore terminal state; opening a new terminal or restarting the terminal profile restores it.
